Q: Rails sanitise and validate input from user for where clause A: <p>I combine multiple scopes. Scope make the code easier to read, understand and to be reused. And when used right Ruby on Rails' query language will sanitise input accordingly</p>
<pre><code># in your models/post.rb
scope :search, -&gt;(title) { where('title LIKE ?', &quot;%#{sanitize_sql_like(title)}%&quot;) if title }
scope :min_cost, -&gt;(cost) { where('? &lt;= cost', cost.presence || 0) }
scope :max_cost, -&gt;(cost) { where('cost &lt;= ?', cost.presence || 999_999_999) }
scope :cost_between, -&gt;(min, max) { min_cost(min).max_cost(max) }
scope :open, -&gt; { where(status: 'open') }
</code></pre>
<p>And then use these scopes like this in your controller:</p>
<pre><code>Post.search(search_params[:keywords])
    .cost_between(search_params[:min], search_params[:max])
    .open
</code></pre>
